<title>USA: Kohl's to open about 30 stores in 1997.</title>
<headline>Kohl's to open about 30 stores in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MENOMONEE FALLS, Wis. 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kohl's Corp, a department store chain, said it plans to open about 30 new stores in 1997, up from 22 opened in 1996.</p>
<p>The retailer plans to enter the Washington, D.C. and Philadelphia markets in the first quarter. It will enter the Pittsburgh market in the third quarter.</p>
<p>A distribution center in Winchester, Va., will open during the summer.</p>
<p>At November 2, 1996, Kohl's operated 150 stores compared with 128 stores at the end of the third quarter a year ago.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
